In the context of transformer models, BOS (Beginning of Sequence) and EOS (End of Sequence) tokens are used to mark the beginning and end of an input or output sequence during the training and generation of text. They are not specific to any particular blockchain or token, but are used as a convention in natural language processing (NLP) tasks.

1. BOS Token: In transformer models, the BOS token is used to indicate the start of a sequence (input or output), helping the model understand where to begin generating or processing text. During training, the input sequence always starts with the BOS token, followed by the actual words or tokens. For example, in a sequence of "The cat sat on the mat", the BOS token will be placed before "The".

