- `max_norm`, `min_count`, and `special_tokens_count`: Parameters related to the filtration process to remove rare words, zero words, and limit the number of special tokens.
- `do_space_tokenization`: A boolean value that determines if the tokenizer should split on space-delimited tokens (useful for handling punctuation and other symbols that may trigger different token combinations for models).

In short, tokenizer config files guide the tokenizer about the structure of the vocabulary and special tokens, and they specify how the model will handle different text scenarios, which makes them crucial for running NLP applications efficiently and accurately.
