5. Resource contention: Limited resources like CPU, memory, and storage can cause performance degradation and service outages. Implement autoscaling to dynamically allocate resources based on demand. Limit the number of concurrent requests at a service level to prevent resource contention.

6. Third-party dependencies: Third-party services like APIs can introduce risks if they fail or are unavailable. Design your system to have minimal dependencies on third-party services. Utilize caching for frequently requested data and implement retries to handle temporary API outages.

